- the user asked for projects “用在你的身上” to reduce token waste, improve tool/logic capability, and strengthen memory -> prefer deployable Codex-compatible integrations with installation/verification over a link roundup; keep the installed subset restrained and auditable. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- The selected non-overlapping stack is RTK for noisy shell output, Serena for symbol-level navigation, Basic Memory for durable local memory, and two focused Superpowers skills. RTK is `C:\Users\25011\.local\bin\rtk.exe`; Serena is pinned in `.codex\config.toml`; Basic Memory project is `C:\Users\25011\Documents\Codex\memory`. Responses API supports `POST /v1/responses/compact` and is lossy/opaque. [Task 1]
- Do not stack Capsule, context-mode, LeanCTX, Headroom, GitNexus full setup, and multiple memory MCPs globally: tool schemas, hooks, startup time, duplicate recall, and prompt overhead can negate compression. Measure provider-billed tokens, success, retries, latency, and correctness; RTK-style output statistics do not establish lower billing. [Task 1]
- On Windows, validate imported UTF-8 skills with `PYTHONUTF8=1`; Basic Memory note search takes a positional query, not `--query`. A `browser-use/plugins` candidate did not support Codex at the time; native Browser Use was callable, so no unknown similarly named plugin was installed. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- `gh` was unavailable (`gh not recognized`) and unauthenticated GitHub release lookup was rate-limited -> verify `gh` early, use authenticated API when metadata matters, and otherwise use repository pages/search plus shallow clones. [Task 1]
- A combined RTK download/extract/install command was blocked by Windows policy -> split download+hash, extraction, copy, and version check. Do not run `rtk init -g --codex` by default because it writes global prompt files. Browser presence requires open/read/click evidence, and API compaction support does not prove automatic current Codex-client compaction. [Task 1]



